family: web-ui
what: flow
transport: v9
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: RFC 3954 (flow v9), RFC 7011 (IPFIX)
does: The values to enter in the device's flow export page so it sends flow records to Woodshed as flow v9 (RFC 3954).
check: Woodshed's Flows view lists the device as an exporter within a minute or two.
placeholders: 
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- This Woodshed doesn't receive flows yet, so nothing will arrive. The port is the flow listener's default.
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Field names differ between devices; some call the collector a target or a server.
- If the page offers sampling, note the rate: Woodshed shows counts as exported and scaled by it.
---- part steps "": In the device's web page, open its flow export settings and enter
Flow export: on
Collector address: 192.0.2.10
Port: 2055 (UDP)
Version: version 9
Interfaces: the ones whose traffic you want to see
Active timeout: 60 seconds (how often long flows are reported)
Template refresh: 60 seconds, if asked
==== text
In the device's web page, open its flow export settings and enter
